msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-measuring-vibration.rst:110
#: 6545690faac94f75b8e2953db3b9c618
msgid "Fly your copter in Stabilize mode and try to maintain a level hover (it doesn't need to be perfectly stable or level)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-measuring-vibration.rst:111
#: aa9485a7d3a94e208b256a8448b0a971
msgid ":ref:`Download the dataflash logs and <common-downloading-and-analyzing-data-logs-in-mission-planner_downloading_logs_via_mavlink>` after the download has completed, use the Mission Planner's \"Review a Log\" button to open the latest file in the log directory (it's last digit will be the Log number you downloaded so in the example above we downloaded Log #1 so the filename will end in 1.log)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-measuring-vibration.rst:116
#: 6adec561b9774c4ab2d60269a8c7846e
msgid "When the Log Browser appears, scroll down until you find any IMU message.  Click on the row's AccX and push **Graph this data** Left button.  Repeat for the AccY and AccZ columns to produce a graph like below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-measuring-vibration.rst:121
#: abb2918c87e94c75b7cccb5618be2b52
msgid "|DiagnosingWithLogs_Vibes|"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-measuring-vibration.rst:133
#: 83e801ee5eda4371849e014c1b3e9dfb
msgid "DiagnosingWithLogs_Vibes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-measuring-vibration.rst:123
#: 17d62ffcfb834edfa49b2731025d6640
msgid "Check the scale on the left and ensure that your vibration levels for the AccX and AccY are between -3 and +3.  For AccZ the acceptable range is -15 to -5.  If it is very close or over these limits you should refer back to the :ref:`Vibration Damping <common-vibration-damping>` page for possible solutions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-measuring-vibration.rst:127
#: 195db36f25d442be8b41025e05409693
msgid "After all the above is complete, go to the Mission Planner's standard parameters page (you may need to press the **Connect** button again) and set the Log Bitmask back to \"Default\".  This is important because especially on the APM logging requires significant CPU resources and it's a waste to log these if they're not really needed."
msgstr ""
